{"item":{"aggregated_output":"{\"changes\":[{\"kind\":\"add\",\"lines\":[\"# eza Python Port Architecture\",\"\",\"## Objective\",\"\",\"Reproduce the observable behavior of eza v0.23.3 for the benchmark scope:\",\"directory listing, long view, tree view, sorting, hidden entries, with colors and\",\"icons disabled. For identical argv, stdin, filesystem, and environment, the\",\"Python command must match the reference process's exit status, stdout bytes,\",\"and stderr bytes.\",\"\",\"## Compatibility boundary\",\"\",\"The port is organized around the same stable behavioral stages as the Rust\",\"application without copying its internal type structure:\",\"\",\"1. `parse_args` recognizes eza flags, short-option clusters, option values,\",\"   positional paths, and parser failures.\",\"2. `scan_inputs` distinguishes explicit files from directories whose children\",\"   should be listed, handles missing paths, and records filesystem metadata.\",\"3. `filter_entries` applies hidden-entry, type, symlink, and ignore rules.\",\"4. `sort_entries` applies eza's stable primary sort, reverse ordering, and\",\"   directory grouping.\",\"5. View renderers produce lines, long tables, recursive blocks, or trees.\",\"6. The process layer writes only to the correct stream and returns eza's exit\",\"   statuses (`0` success, `2` option error, `3` runtime/input error).\",\"\",\"The implementation may use only Python's standard library. It must never call\",\"the reference executable or delegate listing behavior to another CLI.\",\"\",\"## Entrypoint contract\",\"\",\"`compile.sh` is idempotent. It validates the Python source and creates a root\",\"`executable` that is itself Python source, so it is both directly executable on\",\"Unix-like systems and runnable as `python ./executable` by benchmark harnesses.\",\"Compilation removes stale alternative entrypoints before creating the intended\",\"one.\",\"\",\"## Backward-compatibility framework\",\"\",\"`.tura/script/differential.py` creates a deterministic temporary filesystem,\",\"runs a generated invocation matrix against both the official binary and the\",\"Python port, and compares status, stdout, and stderr as bytes. Cases cover each\",\"requested behavior independently and in combinations. Any mismatch prints a\",\"compact unified diff and the exact argv. The verifier is independent of the\",\"implementation and is the primary compatibility oracle.\",\"\",\"## Deliberate scope choices\",\"\",\"Colors and icons are parsed but disabled in the benchmark cases. Git status,\",\"extended attributes, Unix-only owner/group semantics, terminal-only grid\",\"layout, and platform-specific device metadata are outside the stated behavior\",\"area; parser compatibility for harmless adjacent flags is still retained where\",\"practical. No output fixture from the Rust test suite is treated as stronger\",\"evidence than a live differential result on the current host.\"],\"path\":\"architect.md\"},{\"kind\":\"add\",\"lines\":[\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\",\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Byte-for-byte differential verifier for the eza Python port.\\\"\\\"\\\"\",\"\",\"from __future__ import annotations\",\"\",\"import argparse\",\"import difflib\",\"import os\",\"from pathlib import Path\",\"import shutil\",\"import subprocess\",\"import sys\",\"import tempfile\",\"\",\"\",\"ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\",\"REFERENCE_FILE = ROOT / \\\"REFERENCE_BINARY.txt\\\"\",\"\",\"\",\"def make_fixture(base: Path) -> Path:\",\"    root = base / \\\"fixture\\\"\",\"    (root / \\\"alpha-dir\\\" / \\\"nested\\\").mkdir(parents=True)\",\"    (root / \\\"zeta-dir\\\").mkdir()\",\"    files = {\",\"        \\\"Alpha.txt\\\": b\\\"alpha\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"beta.py\\\": b\\\"print('beta')\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"empty\\\": b\\\"\\\",\",\"        \\\"large.bin\\\": b\\\"x\\\" * 1537,\",\"        \\\".hidden\\\": b\\\"hidden\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"alpha-dir/child.txt\\\": b\\\"child\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"alpha-dir/.child-hidden\\\": b\\\"secret\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"alpha-dir/nested/deep.log\\\": b\\\"deep\\\\n\\\",\",\"        \\\"zeta-dir/item.md\\\": b\\\"item\\\\n\\\",\",\"    }\",\"    for relative, content in files.items():\",\"        (root / relative).write_bytes(content)\",\"\",\"    epoch = 1_700_000_000\",\"    for index, path in enumerate(sorted(root.rglob(\\\"*\\\"), key=lambda p: str(p))):\",\"        stamp = epoch + index * 60\",\"        os.utime(path, (stamp, stamp))\",\"    os.utime(root, (epoch, epoch))\",\"    return root\",\"\",\"\",\"def cases(fixture: Path) -> list[list[str]]:\",\"    path = str(fixture)\",\"    return [\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1a\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--sort=size\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1r\\\", \\\"--sort=name\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--sort=extension\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"--group-directories-first\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-l\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-lB\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-lh\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-T\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-Ta\\\", \\\"--level=2\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-lT\\\", \\\"--level=2\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-d1\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-D1\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-f1\\\", path],\",\"        [\\\"--color=never\\\", \\\"--icons=never\\\", \\\"-1\\\", str(fixture / \\\"missing\\\")],\",\"        [\\\"--definitely-invalid\\\"],\",\"    ]\",\"\",\"\",\"def run(command: list[str], argv: list[str], cwd: Path) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[bytes]:\",\"    env = os.environ.copy()\",\"    env.update({\\\"EZA_COLORS\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"NO_COLOR\\\": \\\"1\\\", \\\"COLUMNS\\\": \\\"80\\\"})\",\"    return subprocess.run(\",\"        [*command, *argv],\",\"        cwd=cwd,\",\"        env=env,\",\"        input=b\\\"\\\",\",\"        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\",\"        stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\",\"        check=False,\",\"    )\",\"\",\"\",\"def format_bytes(label: str, value: bytes) -> list[str]:\",\"    return [f\\\"{label}: {line}\\\" for line in value.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", \\\"backslashreplace\\\").splitlines()]\",\"\",\"\",\"def main() -> int:\",\"    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\",\"    parser.add_argument(\\\"--candidate\\\", default=str(ROOT / \\\"eza_port.py\\\"))\",\"    parser.add_argument(\\\"--keep-fixture\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\")\",\"    args = parser.parse_args()\",\"\",\"    reference = Path(REFERENCE_FILE.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").strip())\",\"    candidate = Path(args.candidate).resolve()\",\"    reference_cmd = [str(reference)]\",\"    candidate_cmd = [sys.executable, str(candidate)]\",\"\",\"    temp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\\\"eza-port-diff-\\\"))\",\"    failed = 0\",\"    try:\",\"        fixture = make_fixture(temp)\",\"        for index, argv in enumerate(cases(fixture), 1):\",\"            expected = run(reference_cmd, argv, temp)\",\"            actual = run(candidate_cmd, argv, temp)\",\"            same = (\",\"                expected.returncode == actual.returncode\",\"                and expected.stdout == actual.stdout\",\"                and expected.stderr == actual.stderr\",\"            )\",\"            if same:\",\"                continue\",\"            failed += 1\",\"            print(f\\\"FAIL {index}: {argv!r}\\\")\",\"            print(f\\\"status: expected {expected.returncode}, actual {actual.returncode}\\\")\",\"            expected_lines = format_bytes(\\\"expected\\\", expected.stdout + b\\\"<STDERR>\\\" + expected.stderr)\",\"            actual_lines = format_bytes(\\\"actual\\\", actual.stdout + b\\\"<STDERR>\\\" + actual.stderr)\",\"            print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(expected_lines, actual_lines, lineterm=\\\"\\\")))\",\"        print(f\\\"differential: {len(cases(fixture)) - failed} passed, {failed} failed\\\")\",\"    finally:\",\"        if args.keep_fixture:\",\"            print(f\\\"fixture: {temp}\\\")\",\"        else:\",\"            shutil.rmtree(temp)\",\"    return 1 if failed else 0\",\"\",\"\",\"if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\",\"    raise SystemExit(main())\"],\"path\":\".tura/script/differential.py\"}],\"exit_code\":0,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"Success. Updated files.\"}","changes":[{"kind":"add","lines":["# eza Python Port Architecture","","## Objective","","Reproduce the observable behavior of eza v0.23.3 for the benchmark scope:","directory listing, long view, tree view, sorting, hidden entries, with colors and","icons disabled. For identical argv, stdin, filesystem, and environment, the","Python command must match the reference process's exit status, stdout bytes,","and stderr bytes.","","## Compatibility boundary","","The port is organized around the same stable behavioral stages as the Rust","application without copying its internal type structure:","","1. `parse_args` recognizes eza flags, short-option clusters, option values,","   positional paths, and parser failures.","2. `scan_inputs` distinguishes explicit files from directories whose children","   should be listed, handles missing paths, and records filesystem metadata.","3. `filter_entries` applies hidden-entry, type, symlink, and ignore rules.","4. `sort_entries` applies eza's stable primary sort, reverse ordering, and","   directory grouping.","5. View renderers produce lines, long tables, recursive blocks, or trees.","6. The process layer writes only to the correct stream and returns eza's exit","   statuses (`0` success, `2` option error, `3` runtime/input error).","","The implementation may use only Python's standard library. It must never call","the reference executable or delegate listing behavior to another CLI.","","## Entrypoint contract","","`compile.sh` is idempotent. It validates the Python source and creates a root","`executable` that is itself Python source, so it is both directly executable on","Unix-like systems and runnable as `python ./executable` by benchmark harnesses.","Compilation removes stale alternative entrypoints before creating the intended","one.","","## Backward-compatibility framework","","`.tura/script/differential.py` creates a deterministic temporary filesystem,","runs a generated invocation matrix against both the official binary and the","Python port, and compares status, stdout, and stderr as bytes. Cases cover each","requested behavior independently and in combinations. Any mismatch prints a","compact unified diff and the exact argv. The verifier is independent of the","implementation and is the primary compatibility oracle.","","## Deliberate scope choices","","Colors and icons are parsed but disabled in the benchmark cases. Git status,","extended attributes, Unix-only owner/group semantics, terminal-only grid","layout, and platform-specific device metadata are outside the stated behavior","area; parser compatibility for harmless adjacent flags is still retained where","practical. No output fixture from the Rust test suite is treated as stronger","evidence than a live differential result on the current host."],"path":"architect.md"},{"kind":"add","lines":["#!/usr/bin/env python3","\"\"\"Byte-for-byte differential verifier for the eza Python port.\"\"\"","","from __future__ import annotations","","import argparse","import difflib","import os","from pathlib import Path","import shutil","import subprocess","import sys","import tempfile","","","ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]","REFERENCE_FILE = ROOT / \"REFERENCE_BINARY.txt\"","","","def make_fixture(base: Path) -> Path:","    root = base / \"fixture\"","    (root / \"alpha-dir\" / \"nested\").mkdir(parents=True)","    (root / \"zeta-dir\").mkdir()","    files = {","        \"Alpha.txt\": b\"alpha\\n\",","        \"beta.py\": b\"print('beta')\\n\",","        \"empty\": b\"\",","        \"large.bin\": b\"x\" * 1537,","        \".hidden\": b\"hidden\\n\",","        \"alpha-dir/child.txt\": b\"child\\n\",","        \"alpha-dir/.child-hidden\": b\"secret\\n\",","        \"alpha-dir/nested/deep.log\": b\"deep\\n\",","        \"zeta-dir/item.md\": b\"item\\n\",","    }","    for relative, content in files.items():","        (root / relative).write_bytes(content)","","    epoch = 1_700_000_000","    for index, path in enumerate(sorted(root.rglob(\"*\"), key=lambda p: str(p))):","        stamp = epoch + index * 60","        os.utime(path, (stamp, stamp))","    os.utime(root, (epoch, epoch))","    return root","","","def cases(fixture: Path) -> list[list[str]]:","    path = str(fixture)","    return [","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1a\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--sort=size\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1r\", \"--sort=name\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--sort=extension\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--group-directories-first\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-l\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lB\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lh\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-T\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-Ta\", \"--level=2\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lT\", \"--level=2\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-d1\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-D1\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-f1\", path],","        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", str(fixture / \"missing\")],","        [\"--definitely-invalid\"],","    ]","","","def run(command: list[str], argv: list[str], cwd: Path) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[bytes]:","    env = os.environ.copy()","    env.update({\"EZA_COLORS\": \"\", \"NO_COLOR\": \"1\", \"COLUMNS\": \"80\"})","    return subprocess.run(","        [*command, *argv],","        cwd=cwd,","        env=env,","        input=b\"\",","        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,","        stderr=subprocess.PIPE,","        check=False,","    )","","","def format_bytes(label: str, value: bytes) -> list[str]:","    return [f\"{label}: {line}\" for line in value.decode(\"utf-8\", \"backslashreplace\").splitlines()]","","","def main() -> int:","    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()","    parser.add_argument(\"--candidate\", default=str(ROOT / \"eza_port.py\"))","    parser.add_argument(\"--keep-fixture\", action=\"store_true\")","    args = parser.parse_args()","","    reference = Path(REFERENCE_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").strip())","    candidate = Path(args.candidate).resolve()","    reference_cmd = [str(reference)]","    candidate_cmd = [sys.executable, str(candidate)]","","    temp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"eza-port-diff-\"))","    failed = 0","    try:","        fixture = make_fixture(temp)","        for index, argv in enumerate(cases(fixture), 1):","            expected = run(reference_cmd, argv, temp)","            actual = run(candidate_cmd, argv, temp)","            same = (","                expected.returncode == actual.returncode","                and expected.stdout == actual.stdout","                and expected.stderr == actual.stderr","            )","            if same:","                continue","            failed += 1","            print(f\"FAIL {index}: {argv!r}\")","            print(f\"status: expected {expected.returncode}, actual {actual.returncode}\")","            expected_lines = format_bytes(\"expected\", expected.stdout + b\"<STDERR>\" + expected.stderr)","            actual_lines = format_bytes(\"actual\", actual.stdout + b\"<STDERR>\" + actual.stderr)","            print(\"\\n\".join(difflib.unified_diff(expected_lines, actual_lines, lineterm=\"\")))","        print(f\"differential: {len(cases(fixture)) - failed} passed, {failed} failed\")","    finally:","        if args.keep_fixture:","            print(f\"fixture: {temp}\")","        else:","            shutil.rmtree(temp)","    return 1 if failed else 0","","","if __name__ == \"__main__\":","    raise SystemExit(main())"],"path":".tura/script/differential.py"}],"command":"apply_patch","command_index":0,"command_line":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: architect.md\n+# eza Python Port Architecture\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Reproduce the observable behavior of eza v0.23.3 for the benchmark scope:\n+directory listing, long view, tree view, sorting, hidden entries, with colors and\n+icons disabled. For identical argv, stdin, filesystem, and environment, the\n+Python command must match the reference process's exit status, stdout bytes,\n+and stderr bytes.\n+\n+## Compatibility boundary\n+\n+The port is organized around the same stable behavioral stages as the Rust\n+application without copying its internal type structure:\n+\n+1. `parse_args` recognizes eza flags, short-option clusters, option values,\n+   positional paths, and parser failures.\n+2. `scan_inputs` distinguishes explicit files from directories whose children\n+   should be listed, handles missing paths, and records filesystem metadata.\n+3. `filter_entries` applies hidden-entry, type, symlink, and ignore rules.\n+4. `sort_entries` applies eza's stable primary sort, reverse ordering, and\n+   directory grouping.\n+5. View renderers produce lines, long tables, recursive blocks, or trees.\n+6. The process layer writes only to the correct stream and returns eza's exit\n+   statuses (`0` success, `2` option error, `3` runtime/input error).\n+\n+The implementation may use only Python's standard library. It must never call\n+the reference executable or delegate listing behavior to another CLI.\n+\n+## Entrypoint contract\n+\n+`compile.sh` is idempotent. It validates the Python source and creates a root\n+`executable` that is itself Python source, so it is both directly executable on\n+Unix-like systems and runnable as `python ./executable` by benchmark harnesses.\n+Compilation removes stale alternative entrypoints before creating the intended\n+one.\n+\n+## Backward-compatibility framework\n+\n+`.tura/script/differential.py` creates a deterministic temporary filesystem,\n+runs a generated invocation matrix against both the official binary and the\n+Python port, and compares status, stdout, and stderr as bytes. Cases cover each\n+requested behavior independently and in combinations. Any mismatch prints a\n+compact unified diff and the exact argv. The verifier is independent of the\n+implementation and is the primary compatibility oracle.\n+\n+## Deliberate scope choices\n+\n+Colors and icons are parsed but disabled in the benchmark cases. Git status,\n+extended attributes, Unix-only owner/group semantics, terminal-only grid\n+layout, and platform-specific device metadata are outside the stated behavior\n+area; parser compatibility for harmless adjacent flags is still retained where\n+practical. No output fixture from the Rust test suite is treated as stronger\n+evidence than a live differential result on the current host.\n*** Add File: .tura/script/differential.py\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Byte-for-byte differential verifier for the eza Python port.\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import argparse\n+import difflib\n+import os\n+from pathlib import Path\n+import shutil\n+import subprocess\n+import sys\n+import tempfile\n+\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n+REFERENCE_FILE = ROOT / \"REFERENCE_BINARY.txt\"\n+\n+\n+def make_fixture(base: Path) -> Path:\n+    root = base / \"fixture\"\n+    (root / \"alpha-dir\" / \"nested\").mkdir(parents=True)\n+    (root / \"zeta-dir\").mkdir()\n+    files = {\n+        \"Alpha.txt\": b\"alpha\\n\",\n+        \"beta.py\": b\"print('beta')\\n\",\n+        \"empty\": b\"\",\n+        \"large.bin\": b\"x\" * 1537,\n+        \".hidden\": b\"hidden\\n\",\n+        \"alpha-dir/child.txt\": b\"child\\n\",\n+        \"alpha-dir/.child-hidden\": b\"secret\\n\",\n+        \"alpha-dir/nested/deep.log\": b\"deep\\n\",\n+        \"zeta-dir/item.md\": b\"item\\n\",\n+    }\n+    for relative, content in files.items():\n+        (root / relative).write_bytes(content)\n+\n+    epoch = 1_700_000_000\n+    for index, path in enumerate(sorted(root.rglob(\"*\"), key=lambda p: str(p))):\n+        stamp = epoch + index * 60\n+        os.utime(path, (stamp, stamp))\n+    os.utime(root, (epoch, epoch))\n+    return root\n+\n+\n+def cases(fixture: Path) -> list[list[str]]:\n+    path = str(fixture)\n+    return [\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1a\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--sort=size\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1r\", \"--sort=name\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--sort=extension\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", \"--group-directories-first\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-l\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lB\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lh\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-T\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-Ta\", \"--level=2\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-lT\", \"--level=2\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-d1\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-D1\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-f1\", path],\n+        [\"--color=never\", \"--icons=never\", \"-1\", str(fixture / \"missing\")],\n+        [\"--definitely-invalid\"],\n+    ]\n+\n+\n+def run(command: list[str], argv: list[str], cwd: Path) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[bytes]:\n+    env = os.environ.copy()\n+    env.update({\"EZA_COLORS\": \"\", \"NO_COLOR\": \"1\", \"COLUMNS\": \"80\"})\n+    return subprocess.run(\n+        [*command, *argv],\n+        cwd=cwd,\n+        env=env,\n+        input=b\"\",\n+        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n+        stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n+        check=False,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+def format_bytes(label: str, value: bytes) -> list[str]:\n+    return [f\"{label}: {line}\" for line in value.decode(\"utf-8\", \"backslashreplace\").splitlines()]\n+\n+\n+def main() -> int:\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--candidate\", default=str(ROOT / \"eza_port.py\"))\n+    parser.add_argument(\"--keep-fixture\", action=\"store_true\")\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+\n+    reference = Path(REFERENCE_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").strip())\n+    candidate = Path(args.candidate).resolve()\n+    reference_cmd = [str(reference)]\n+    candidate_cmd = [sys.executable, str(candidate)]\n+\n+    temp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"eza-port-diff-\"))\n+    failed = 0\n+    try:\n+        fixture = make_fixture(temp)\n+        for index, argv in enumerate(cases(fixture), 1):\n+            expected = run(reference_cmd, argv, temp)\n+            actual = run(candidate_cmd, argv, temp)\n+            same = (\n+                expected.returncode == actual.returncode\n+                and expected.stdout == actual.stdout\n+                and expected.stderr == actual.stderr\n+            )\n+            if same:\n+                continue\n+            failed += 1\n+            print(f\"FAIL {index}: {argv!r}\")\n+            print(f\"status: expected {expected.returncode}, actual {actual.returncode}\")\n+            expected_lines = format_bytes(\"expected\", expected.stdout + b\"<STDERR>\" + expected.stderr)\n+            actual_lines = format_bytes(\"actual\", actual.stdout + b\"<STDERR>\" + actual.stderr)\n+            print(\"\\n\".join(difflib.unified_diff(expected_lines, actual_lines, lineterm=\"\")))\n+        print(f\"differential: {len(cases(fixture)) - failed} passed, {failed} failed\")\n+    finally:\n+        if args.keep_fixture:\n+            print(f\"fixture: {temp}\")\n+        else:\n+            shutil.rmtree(temp)\n+    return 1 if failed else 0\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    raise SystemExit(main())\n*** End Patch","command_type":"apply_patch","id":"runtime-18c0fdbb0849ced4.tool.command_run:call_OlInVCsdDSq8VIP8BZJnxOkK:0","provider_tool_call_id":"call_OlInVCsdDSq8VIP8BZJnxOkK","status":"completed","step":1,"type":"file_change"},"type":"item.completed"}
{"item":{"aggregated_output":"{\"exit_code\":0,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"Total output lines: 243\\n\\nTotal output lines: 361\\n\\n// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2024 Christina Sørensen\\r\\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2\\r\\n//\\r\\n// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2023-2024 Christina Sørensen, eza contributors\\r\\n// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2014 Benjamin Sago\\r\\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\\r\\n//! A general parser for command-line options.\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! exa uses its own hand-rolled parser for command-line options. It supports\\r\\n//! the following syntax:\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! - Long options: `--inode`, `--grid`\\r\\n//! - Long options with values: `--sort size`, `--level=4`\\r\\n//! - Short options: `-i`, `-G`\\r\\n//! - Short options with values: `-ssize`, `-L=4`\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! These values can be mixed and matched: `exa -lssize --grid`. If you’ve used\\r\\n//! other command-line programs, then hopefully it’ll work much like them.\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! Because exa already has its own files for the help text, shell completions,\\r\\n//! man page, and readme, so it can get away with having the options parser do\\r\\n//! very little: all it really needs to do is parse a slice of strings.\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! ## UTF-8 and `OsStr`\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! The parser uses `OsStr` as its string type. This is necessary for exa to\\r\\n//! list files that have invalid UTF-8 in their names: by treating file paths\\r\\n//! as bytes with no encoding, a file can be specified on the command-line and\\r\\n//! be looked up without having to be encoded into a `str` first.\\r\\n//!\\r\\n//! It also avoids the overhead of checking for invalid UTF-8 when parsing\\r\\n//! command-line options, as all the options and their values (such as\\r\\n//! `--sort size`) are guaranteed to just be 8-bit ASCII.\\r\\n\\r\\nuse std::ffi::{OsStr, OsString};\\r\\nuse std::fmt;\\r\\n\\r\\nuse crate::options::error::{Choices, OptionsError};\\r\\n\\r\\n/// A **short argument** is a single ASCII